2026-08-08T02:46:57.4699034Z [36;1m# standard flags R selects per version (e.g. -std=gnu2x for C, -std=gnu++17[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4699507Z [36;1m# / -std=gnu++20 for C++); a plain "CC = ccache gcc" override would drop[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4699951Z [36;1m# them and silently downgrade the standard across the version matrix.[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4700407Z [36;1m# Inference uses an empty user Makevars so we always read the pristine[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4700802Z [36;1m# Makeconf defaults, never a value we just wrote.[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4701194Z [36;1m# Note: the versioned switches (CXX11..CXX23) intentionally come out as[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4701637Z [36;1m# bare "g++" with no -std flag. R keeps the standard in a separate[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4702078Z [36;1m# CXXnnSTD variable (CXX17STD = -std=gnu++17, ...) and applies it on top[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4702534Z [36;1m# at compile time, so wrapping only CXXnn with ccache is correct and we[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4702902Z [36;1m# must NOT pin -std here ourselves.[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4703162Z [36;1mempty_makevars="$(mktemp)"[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4703690Z [36;1mfor var in CC CXX CXX11 CXX14 CXX17 CXX20 CXX23; do[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4704147Z [36;1m  val="$(R_MAKEVARS_USER="$empty_makevars" R CMD config "$var" 2>/dev/null || true)"[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4704527Z [36;1m  if [ -n "$val" ]; then[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4704776Z [36;1m    echo "$var = ccache $val" >> ~/.R/Makevars[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4705030Z [36;1m  fi[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4705187Z [36;1mdone[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4705363Z [36;1mrm -f "$empty_makevars"[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4705697Z [36;1m[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4705959Z [36;1m# Compile on every core the runner has, not the two this used to pin.[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4706418Z [36;1m# Standard GitHub-hosted Linux runners have been 4-vCPU since 2024, so[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4706872Z [36;1m# -j2 left half the box idle through the phase that dominates a build:[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4707299Z [36;1m# measured on a 4-core box, 8 vendored unity objects with ccache[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4707719Z [36;1m# disabled take 70.8 s at -j2 and 43.1 s at -j4 -- 1.64x, at identical[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4708354Z [36;1m# user time. Peak RSS per unity object is ~834 MB, so four in flight is[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4708709Z [36;1m# ~3.3 GB of the runner's 16 GB.[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4709053Z [36;1m# detectCores() can return NA on exotic platforms; fall back to the old[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4709507Z [36;1m# value there. `--as-cran` sets _R_CHECK_LIMIT_CORES_, but that polices[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4709968Z [36;1m# the *package's* runtime parallelism, not compilation, so this is safe.[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4710549Z [36;1mncores="$(Rscript --vanilla -e 'n <- parallel::detectCores(); cat(if (is.na(n) || n < 1) 2L else as.integer(n))')"[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4711063Z [36;1mecho "MAKEFLAGS = -j${ncores}" >> ~/.R/Makevars[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4711372Z [36;1mecho "===== generated ~/.R/Makevars ====="[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4711633Z [36;1mcat ~/.R/Makevars[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4711863Z [36;1mecho "==================================="[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4712104Z [36;1m[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4712363Z [36;1mecho 'CCACHE_SLOPPINESS=locale,time_macros' | tee -a $GITHUB_ENV[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4712695Z [36;1m[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4712953Z [36;1m# Do NOT export UserNM here, however tempting the `UserNM=true` trick[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4713429Z [36;1m# from AGENTS.md looks. It is a development shortcut, not a CI setting.[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4713767Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4713963Z [36;1m# R takes the nm program from $UserNM in[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4714325Z [36;1m# tools:::read_symbols_from_object_file, and that function serves two[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4714760Z [36;1m# callers, not one: building `symbols.rds` at install time (which[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4715132Z [36;1m# src/Makevars puts on the `all:` target), *and*[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4715513Z [36;1m# tools:::check_so_symbols scanning the built .so during `R CMD check`.[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4715964Z [36;1m# Pointing nm at `true` blinds the second one, so the check finds no[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4716406Z [36;1m# symbols at all and reports "Found no calls to 'R_registerRoutines',[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4716859Z [36;1m# 'R_useDynamicSymbols'" -- a NOTE, and with error_on = "note" a failed[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4717299Z [36;1m# check on a package that registers its routines perfectly well.[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4717617Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4718073Z [36;1m# It is not worth scoping to the installs either: measured, the sweep is[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4718520Z [36;1m# ~0.25 s per 90 MB of unstripped objects, so ~10-20 s for the whole[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4718934Z [36;1m# ~2.5 GB tree -- under 5% of a commit's floor, against a footgun that[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4719278Z [36;1m# silently weakens a CRAN check.[0m
2026-08-08T02:46:57.4719507Z [36;1m[0m
